1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,400
The Combination Lock

2
00:00:15,599 --> 00:00:17,080
Ah! He's home!

3
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,240
Nolik, are you here?

4
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,199
Stop your hiding.

5
00:00:28,679 --> 00:00:29,960
I'll still find you.

6
00:00:30,839 --> 00:00:32,560
Nolik, is that you?

7
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:35,240
Hey, come on! That's not fair!

8
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:36,320
You saw!

9
00:00:36,719 --> 00:00:37,719
Let me go again!

10
00:00:37,719 --> 00:00:38,799
I don't want to!

11
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:42,960
You want me to play hide and seek when I got a brand new game to play with?

12
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:44,439
Where is it?

13
00:00:44,519 --> 00:00:46,480
I don't see it anywhere in the room.

14
00:00:46,799 --> 00:00:48,480
I took it to school with me.

15
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:50,000
For what reason?

16
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:51,439
To show it off.

17
00:00:57,079 --> 00:00:58,960
Wow! Awesome game!

18
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:02,719
Tom Thomas! Can I play your game?

19
00:01:02,799 --> 00:01:05,719
Uh-uh! Because I'm not done playing with it yet.

20
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:09,400
Now just try asking me to do some favor for you!

21
00:01:10,239 --> 00:01:12,560
Hmm, wait, was it a three or a four? Hmm.

22
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,240
It could have been five!

23
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:16,680
I forgot!

24
00:01:17,879 --> 00:01:18,840
What about?

25
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:20,760
I forgot the combination.

26
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:23,159
And now I can't even do my homework.

27
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:26,000
Everything I need to finish is inside of there.

28
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:28,400
I'm not climbing in to find out your homework!

29
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:29,640
Don't even ask me!

30
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:33,000
Tom Thomas, why do you look so upset?

31
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:37,360
Uh, the code for the lock. I don't remember it.

32
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:38,640
Don't you worry!

33
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:42,040
We'll open it! I know all about a code lock!

34
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:48,200
A simple code lock is built with a few discs that have numbers on them.

35
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:52,200
In the center of each disc is a hole with a notch.

36
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:57,160
When all of the discs are turned so their notches line up in a straight row,

37
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:59,879
the lock's pin can slide out freely.

38
00:02:04,599 --> 00:02:06,799
And to get the notches to line up,

39
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:11,240
just turn the discs to the lock's code and the lock will open.

40
00:02:11,759 --> 00:02:13,079
It's that simple!

41
00:02:15,319 --> 00:02:18,079
Looks like we've got to take a look inside the lock.

42
00:02:20,039 --> 00:02:20,960
Ah, I see.

43
00:02:21,199 --> 00:02:22,800
Nolik, where are you?

44
00:02:22,919 --> 00:02:24,120
There's work to do.

45
00:02:24,439 --> 00:02:25,479
I won't do it.

46
00:02:25,479 --> 00:02:27,879
I'm not going to help such a greedy boy!

47
00:02:28,079 --> 00:02:30,000
Nolik, won't you help me out here?

48
00:02:30,119 --> 00:02:32,199
And I won't be so greedy anymore!

49
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:34,719
Alright, you broke me down.

50
00:02:35,399 --> 00:02:38,599
Omi, as soon as we're done, you're going to let me play with the game.

51
00:02:38,599 --> 00:02:39,199
Right!

52
00:02:43,799 --> 00:02:46,039
There's no room in here!

53
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:48,799
Hang in there! We'll start turning the discs one at a time

54
00:02:48,799 --> 00:02:50,959
and you yell stop when they're lined up.

55
00:02:51,599 --> 00:02:52,280
Stop!

56
00:02:52,399 --> 00:02:53,879
Turn the next one now!

57
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,519
Stop!

58
00:02:56,799 --> 00:02:57,439
Stop!

59
00:02:58,719 --> 00:03:00,159
Now try!

60
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:03,519
Yes!

61
00:03:04,079 --> 00:03:04,919
Alley-oop!

62
00:03:05,319 --> 00:03:06,400
Tideesh!

63
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,799
Hurrah!

64
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:11,199
And your code was really simple!

65
00:03:11,519 --> 00:03:12,680
Way too simple!

66
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:19,439
The secret numbers and letters that you use to lock something up

67
00:03:19,439 --> 00:03:21,439
are called the code or the password.

68
00:03:21,439 --> 00:03:24,719
And to make sure your password is a really good one,

69
00:03:24,719 --> 00:03:26,719
here are some things you should know.

70
00:03:26,719 --> 00:03:31,520
Never choose a password that's really simple for someone else to guess.

71
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:36,639
Like one with numbers or letters that are all the same or are all in order.

72
00:03:36,879 --> 00:03:41,120
It's also a bad idea to make a password out of your birthdate or name.

73
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:45,360
It's better to think of a password that's a bit more complicated.

74
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:48,479
And don't forget your password once you come up with it.

75
00:03:48,479 --> 00:03:53,280
Write down your password on a piece of paper and keep it in a safe place,

76
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:55,840
but don't show it to anybody else.

77
00:03:56,039 --> 00:03:59,439
And then, if you happen to forget your code or password,

78
00:03:59,439 --> 00:04:03,399
you'll be able to remember it with the help of that piece of paper.

79
00:04:12,199 --> 00:04:15,039
And why did you ever put a lock on your backpack?

80
00:04:15,159 --> 00:04:17,599
I was hiding the game from the other kids.

81
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:19,800
Then why did you take it to school today?

82
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:22,720
I wanted to show it off to my class.

83
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:24,200
And did you show it?

84
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:27,760
No way! If they would have seen it, they'd be like,

85
00:04:27,879 --> 00:04:30,080
I want to use it! I want to play!

86
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:32,960
And so you hid it and didn't show it to anybody?

87
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:34,480
Not to anyone.

88
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:36,960
Then why take it to school, silly?

89
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:40,280
To show it off there.

90
00:04:40,439 --> 00:04:42,320
You're just some show-off!

91
00:04:42,439 --> 00:04:44,280
You're just some greedy…

92
00:04:44,879 --> 00:04:46,760
Oops! Sorry, once greedy boy!

93
00:04:46,759 --> 00:04:48,360
Will you let us play now?

94
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:52,719
Play away.

95
00:05:02,879 --> 00:05:04,480
We're not bothering you, are we?

96
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:07,079
Can you jump a little easier?

97
00:05:07,159 --> 00:05:08,879
You're shaking the whole desk.

